Z||000000||FieroPerformance||08-05-2001||10:07 PM||||I am finally rebuilding my engine. It should be out of the car in about a day or two. I want to rebuild it with performance parts and get the most out of it that I can without losing reliability.<P>I picked the following parts from <A HREF="http://www.spoperformanceparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.spoperformanceparts.com</A>  and I was wondering if anyone could tell me if they will work well and if they are the best choices:<P>Cam shaft       P/N   12364059<BR>Roller Rockers  P/N   24504436<BR>Oil pump        P/N   10051104<BR>Valve Spring    P/N   330585<BR>Spring retainer P/N   330586<BR>Timing Chain    P/N   14102670<P>I am thinking about getting high compression pistons but I can't find any on the GM site.<P>I also plan on buying the following:<P>Low temp thermostat<BR>Underdrive pulley     (fierostore)<BR>Stainless vavles      (fierostore)<BR>Free flow cat         (rodney dickman)<BR>Accel 300 Ignition    (summit racing)<BR>Fuel pressure regulator<P>I will probably have the headers ported and polished also.<P>Any help or advice I can get would be greatly apreciated.<P>Thanks,<BR>-Charlie<BR>-----<BR>jackalrr@hotmail.com<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic.jpg"> ||||reg||5
